===Noun===
{{en-noun|sg=[[tree]] [[lawn]]}}

# {{context|US|Midwestern}} The [[grass]]y area between the [[sidewalk]] and the [[street]].

====Usage notes====
This term has significant dialectical differences, and some dialects and idiolects do not include a term for this area,<ref name="tls">[http://tls.timesonline.co.uk/article/0,,25362-1923881,00.html The triumph of slang], John A. C. Greppin, 2002-02-01</ref> often using a [[circumlocution]].<ref>[http://www.slate.com/id/2086909/ The world’s worst hobby], by Emily Yoffe, ''[[w:Slate.com|Slate]],'' refers to the area as “the grassy strip that runs along the street side of many D.C. sidewalks”.</ref>

